# Duta zephyr app options.
config DUTA_SNIFF
	bool "Build the BLE advertising sniffer variant"
	depends on !BT && !DUTA_SNIFF_154 && !DUTA_SNIFF_MULTI
	help
	  Replace the UART DATA bridge with a raw-radio BLE advertising sniffer
	  (nRF only). The radio is driven directly — incompatible with the BLE
	  controller (BT) — to capture advertising PDUs on channels 37/38/39. DATA
	  becomes a stream of captured-packet records (kind = ble-sniff). Select via
	  `-DEXTRA_CONF_FILE=overlay-sniff.conf`.

config DUTA_SNIFF_154
	bool "Build the IEEE 802.15.4 (Zigbee/Thread) sniffer variant"
	depends on !BT && !DUTA_SNIFF_MULTI
	help
	  Replace the UART DATA bridge with a raw-radio IEEE 802.15.4 sniffer (nRF
	  only). The radio is driven directly in its 802.15.4 mode to capture frames
	  on channels 11-26 (Zigbee and Thread share this PHY/MAC). DATA becomes a
	  stream of captured-frame records (kind = ieee802154). One radio, so this is
	  mutually exclusive with the BLE sniffer. Select via
	  `-DEXTRA_CONF_FILE=overlay-sniff154.conf`.

config DUTA_SNIFF_MULTI
	bool "Build the unified runtime-switchable sniffer (BLE + 802.15.4)"
	depends on !BT
	help
	  Compile BOTH raw-radio sniffer backends into one image and switch the live
	  PHY at runtime via CFG_SET key 0x14 (DATA kind): 4 = BLE advertising
	  (channels 37/38/39), 7 = IEEE 802.15.4 (channels 11-26 — Zigbee, Thread,
	  and Matter-over-Thread, which share the PHY; the Wireshark dissector tells
	  them apart). DATA_DESC reflects the active link type so the extcap picks the
	  matching DLT. One nRF radio, so incompatible with the BLE controller (BT).
	  Boots in BLE mode. Select via `-DEXTRA_CONF_FILE=overlay-sniff-multi.conf`.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
